englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3cc1fdf3914f559cf090e0119a1aaa5ec36ec2c488392950f842ed107f157dcf","compact":"adc16c44b93293b809914b7e707d663c492d9df91089ad86700fb89af95ef55b","nasal":"adc16c44b93293b809914b7e707d663c492d9df91089ad86700fb89af95ef55b"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":7,"english":"Arriving there cried he where is Şītā? Neither did the world of creatures nor the river Godāvarī apprise Rāma of Sītā's being carried away by the Lord of Rākşasas worthy of being slain.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.691,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"44cde6dff6fa27dcf51ba4cf8a2cfe5c9481365cdfeaa1ee7d06eba5aae67e48","compact":"3f961e39f5c847eafffc447107a6d63c9f8bc93ab1ed92e0af6053059a291a91","nasal":"045bdb517affc604c7a1f639df3cf8335337872f378ecfd3325ce7fa54e6fd25"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":8,"english":"Thinking of the terrible figure and monstrous action of that vicious-souled Råvaņa, that river did not dare relate to him anything about Sītā, albeit appointed by the creatures to relate the story concerning her and accosted by Răma in piteous accents.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.594,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"79e7c9c252a3d97b2f72ec02250c0d247c9334aba732a06983a85f0d7e1b2e2c","compact":"38ece67ebd4b38b29d276946f089f9504057b717236c732e65fe4420b99a78b2","nasal":"38ece67ebd4b38b29d276946f089f9504057b717236c732e65fe4420b99a78b2"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":9,"english":"Thinking of the terrible figure and monstrous action of that vicious-souled Råvaņa, that river did not dare relate to him anything about Sītā, albeit appointed by the creatures to relate the story concerning her and accosted by Răma in piteous accents.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.672,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4c1596371048cb088d9b278cabe1b20e643b097450f33bec92041692ea19471","compact":"722d885937ec2dd385b5ffcd4fb33a9059af550519baae70daa3c7d20183ed84","nasal":"722d885937ec2dd385b5ffcd4fb33a9059af550519baae70daa3c7d20183ed84"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":10,"english":"Being thus disappointed by the river in beholding Sītā, Răma racked with her separation spoke to Lakşmaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b91531b154a51adf155b05ba8ffdaf222b086bfe7e90c7053451cc8e86c7a5ef","compact":"125239e942448787729aa1ac61d3ae35ea4e850f5742d58a308ffd50877b41da","nasal":"125239e942448787729aa1ac61d3ae35ea4e850f5742d58a308ffd50877b41da"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":11,"english":"O you of auspicious looks, this river Godāvarī dose give no reply. But O Laksmana, returning without her what shall I say to Janaka and Vaidehi's mother?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.932,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b86f158c74df732163a04d92bcd3fd0f6b0c7cce7bbef44beed6564f11ab4448","compact":"d03c930d0f4e5d1f553af84b28c601aed422368b2035ce48f762eb8a417da5a1","nasal":"d03c930d0f4e5d1f553af84b28c601aed422368b2035ce48f762eb8a417da5a1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":12,"english":"Where has that Vaidehi gone who used to assuage my grief who had been deprived of kingdom and living in this forest on wild fruits and vegetables? Nights shall appear too long to me, keeping late liquors being deprived of my kinsmen and relatives and not beholding Vaidehi.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.789,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"98946e49325bb4b511e664e10a0648ccf90bf962830e47a601e7d8303447dc50","compact":"e054dcf4552d7d33c14b19722935a725b3ea754f51d16e82c33aadc87f2ef2b9","nasal":"e054dcf4552d7d33c14b19722935a725b3ea754f51d16e82c33aadc87f2ef2b9"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":13,"english":"I can range this Mandakini, this Janasthāna and this Pasravana hill if I can find Sītā there.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.469,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"758b9848e96550bc23f148221e58c7dec0318606ea19910c8115fb1d919fbb2e","compact":"d73b1173a4a9ac9b19134eb02a4d35688e47e8e84c97af256ced3a0631bda387","nasal":"165bdb8afe40e07f205481e4117f9806094edb36cff3fbfed1583b59dd2988af"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":14,"english":"I can range this Mandakini, this Janasthāna and this Pasravana hill if I can find Sītā there.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdi