":{"sanskritLocator":"3060017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8a95e66ec92c31a35f42e627154aea8df7fef1269fd070600005e31831c07404","compact":"4579d684c8ccb9eb2e18287aa1781bea5105039a7eb63bf8fc73dc9682349720","nasal":"4579d684c8ccb9eb2e18287aa1781bea5105039a7eb63bf8fc73dc9682349720"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":18,"english":"Having spoken these words to Lakşmaņa, the best of men, the virtuous-souled Rāma, of mighty arms, addressed the mountain in front of him containing many fountains. Exceedingly wroth he accosted the mountain like to a lion addressing a little deer, saying Show me my graceful Sītā hued like gold before I crush down your summits. Being thus addressed by Rāma on Maithili's account the mountain did not show him Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.486,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-20","DUTT-3-64-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6ebae6de73b09fd5a94e22ecce6e4b0f1041801d36b0a13481c9ffa8ee2896d7","compact":"4c77560cc97fdb1d4e07bba06df69a7f7c73afaa5a13c4519bd1cb60d3e7c822","nasal":"4c77560cc97fdb1d4e07bba06df69a7f7c73afaa5a13c4519bd1cb60d3e7c822"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":19,"english":"Exceedingly wroth he accosted the mountain like to a lion addressing a little deer, saying Show me my graceful Sītā hued like gold before I crush down your summits. Being thus addressed by Rāma on Maithili's account the mountain did not show him Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9fd7201f57a6401d98605c834fd3592d553e40a5981ce7f27988a45947655209","compact":"0bfc32b73ee3052183a3cdc1b92a4213b426b5c7433ec0d8214cd1593a27674b","nasal":"0bfc32b73ee3052183a3cdc1b92a4213b426b5c7433ec0d8214cd1593a27674b"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":20,"english":"Again addressed him Rāma—You shall by the fire of my arrows, be reduced to ashes-your twigs and leaves shall be totally destroyed and no one shall resort to you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060020","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e15bb462fb0a0328a33633480d7533263de7501865745abcab1639434a916bdb","compact":"9d3e74f6bb394209e26773f825abe38c34ff53f8e5e6b6283ed3860707a355ca","nasal":"9d3e74f6bb394209e26773f825abe38c34ff53f8e5e6b6283ed3860707a355ca"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-21","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":21,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, I shall dry up this river Godāvari if it tell me not about Sītā having a moon-like countenance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060021","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"464491af19957cdb2f04e4faa57a030b33012754200600e5dc2c8baa37acc541","compact":"a1d7bca28e0c63206f7a819e0b7925fceac0f55d58fc536f4bdf1b48627b10ab","nasal":"0d439472d5869e9d3f7916a6f7fc4e69a02c950f05e2c61e9dd758805e8cb0e1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-22","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":22,"english":"Rāma, exceedingly wroth, cast his looks around as if desiring to burn everything with his eyes and beheld footprints of the Räkşasas on the earth as well as those of Sītā moving wildly hither and thither, terrified and desirous to see Rāma, while pursued by the Rākşasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.935,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060022","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f9dc6af593c6401d38dafe7c57a3bb9b8d4e37aeb867425a8a03033225fc855b","compact":"d83dfab76d27e587ad50c3b47665f926c3d989f9e7d97d3f11b807dd171b1414","nasal":"1c427a21c40593898f81fc9392117279f48dba078a75d290c5a59beb0b7f602c"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-23","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":23,"english":"Beholding these foot marks, the snapped bow, the quiver and the chariot broken into many pieces, Rāma, terrified spoke to his dear brother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060023","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f602277b1afe4bbaedcb9d48192bf68c7ba75b0c2ac69470b83424e3d57bcc7e","compact":"c506f3233373e6e158d40b1ef1d42297b984c3c2162f2710d21ebd25629cc699","nasal":"8ce8a7384cc3bd41d545c4d4caade526f3884145bb3013caacaf4f2064050a5d"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-24","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":24,"english":"Behold O, Laksmana, the remnants of Vaidehi's golden ornaments, strewn hither and thither, and diverse garlands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060024","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"017fe132087c5dcbc5e4aec46c78c1ba483f5f12df95ea3821419929f016301c","compact":"2b7273b4a5ac901b4b2c7d148ab92c0a4b44b4d7471606a80f68c3dcedab6980","nasal":"bf88996ff79dc7bba4b00e9158ff58b4d32e47c2139dee6e2efbd7b941fa6523"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-25","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":25,"english":"Behold O Saumitrī, the earth covered with drops of blood resembling golden drops.","ali