rse":47,"english":"Stretching the bow to my ears I shall make the world, for Sita's sake, void of Pisacas and Raks asas with my arrows incapable of being withstood by created beings.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.845,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-46"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060047","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"224ae430fefbd9d1337156011faa66874fe293d2fa8843d095f0a37fae64e48d","compact":"f16e7555433ed9c07772a83bda87a9b96b1d202803d3588eb1577082eeb390f6","nasal":"f16e7555433ed9c07772a83bda87a9b96b1d202803d3588eb1577082eeb390f6"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-48","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":48,"english":"To-day shall the celestials behold the power of my arrows coursing a long distance shot through my ire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.845,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-47"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060048","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"729702cead0debeb8a5308885c9d0ed1734ea20ccfd98d1a30cdd9630b4b3723","compact":"9dd6ce3b0cb1ac277656b049e2c27141024b0dde4be60213bc8db8588eef3e70","nasal":"42ff7ea230163dc3e9c02eb1f9a9c0ec3b963e9a29d8598103735f01e969531b"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-49","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":49,"english":"Three worlds, destroyed on account of my wrath, celestials, Sanavas, Pisacas or Raks asas,-none shall be saved.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-48"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060049","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e48611f883aeff0d3a88ee3bdac3d820711bfc0025ce9b34dc6344906b20615","compact":"71306d11360dd530ddf8dae09e3a60f76870d2b9c161b496f4e2e5bc11c28962","nasal":"b6e87d208ef9100d3415a686776994e0d497918c66ff497b084171323c2b71fe"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-50","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":50,"english":"The dwellings of the celestials, Asuras, Yaks as and Rākşasas shall fall down sundered by my arrows into diverse pieces. I shall dislodge the whole world by my arrows. If the celestials do not give me back my Vaidehī dead or carried away or as she was before, I shall destroy the whole world mobile or immobile and disturb all with my arrows until i see her.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.44,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-49","DUTT-3-64-50"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060050","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"389dbf55d143a521ca112946866e6dc446d4551b2d86be85da2545866145fe90","compact":"030cc703b9b2270ae63b970594290f571bd833f7d46b8dfa94092b1ce6cdf3e7","nasal":"ebf7a75294b557c081ac7b7bfa8600c340756d592703082799c579ee4d07f32e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-51","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":51,"english":"O Lakşınaņa none shall be able to withstand me, who am inflamed with rage, as debility consequent on old age, death, time, duty are incapable of being averted from their destined ends by the animals.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-64-54"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3060051","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f256329c83cae96d15f14f04d8859a6887f0821a2c35d4e42505896bb6b5f60d","compact":"a9ab0fd1b0d610625ff5f3b92afa6c2b80c2d484ef67d10dc4dd8dee17808852","nasal":"41dfd6091891d7343e0a0dd89092889f5197e9a18f64c11f0aa302a7d4bdc2fa"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-60-52","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":60,"verse":52,"english":"I shall bring about a mighty revolution in the world containing the celestials Gandharvas, human beings, Pannagas and the mountains, if I do not get back, in her pristine beau